    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nSince my last upgrade (on debian) to 0.12.3-4, my block-cursor (in urxvt, xterm) blinks after I exit nvim.\n\nI tried all sorts of vim config options to fix it from there: (e.g. \n```\nau VimLeave,VimSuspend * set guicursor=a:block-blinkoff0`)\nautocmd VimLeave * silent !echo -ne \"\\e[2 q\"\n...\n```\n\nI managed to work around with adding this to my `$PROMPT_COMMAND`: `    echo -ne \"\\e[2 q\" # set block cursor`.\n\nThis workaround does not work e.g. in `mutt`, hence I open this bug.\n\nWhile reporting, I found that my `$TERM` values (`rxvt-unicode-256color`, `rxvt-256color`) create the problem.\nChanging it to `xterm-256color` also works around this. However, since `rxvt-...256color` settings work for `vim` and previous `neovim`s, I guess this still is a bug. In particular since `mutt` is still affected.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\n:q\nObserve blinking block cursor\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nObserve cursor in its previous state\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.3 Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1761786044\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, VIM - Vi IMproved 9.2 (2026 Feb 14, compiled Jun 27 2026 18:49:09)\n\n### Operating system/version\n\ndebian/trixie\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nxterm-410, urxvt-9.31\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nrxvt-unicode-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nDebian package",
