            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If you don't want Nvim to change your terminal cursor, disable 'guicursor' by unsetting it in your config:\n\n    :set guicursor=\n\n\nThat ability to \"disable Nvim cursor behavior\" is what #40249 enabled.\n\nAnd even before #40249 , Nvim always emits the standard \"reset cursor\" sequence, which only works if your terminal actually supports it. But it wouldn't suprirse me if rxvt doesn't support it, because rxvt is the Internet Explorer of terminal emulators.",
